'''Group moderation''' in VRChat provides community leaders and appointed staff with the essential tools required to maintain a safe, welcoming, and organized environment within their custom groups. By utilizing these integrated features, group owners can establish clear behavioral expectations and enforce community guidelines directly inside their instances. This dedicated framework helps minimize disruptions, protects members from harassment, and ensures that group-affiliated worlds remain enjoyable for all participants.

At the core of this system is a robust hierarchy of roles and permissions that can be customized to fit the specific needs of any community. Owners can designate trusted users as administrators or moderators, granting them specific capabilities such as inviting members, warnings management, and instance moderation. These tiered permission levels allow large groups to distribute administrative duties efficiently, ensuring that active staff are always available to handle issues without compromising the overall security of the group's highest settings.

When disruptive behavior occurs, moderators have access to a suite of real-time tools to resolve conflicts instantly, including options to kick, mute, or permanently ban problematic users from group instances. Additionally, the system tracks these interventions within a centralized moderation log, allowing management teams to review actions taken by staff to ensure consistency and accountability. Through the combination of proactive role management and reactive disciplinary tools, group moderation forms the backbone of stable, long-term community building on the platform.